      "• Coarse and fine spiral twisted fiber mesh structure : High dust holding coarse denier melt-spun filter material has a unique designable coarse and fine fiber alternating structure, in which the coarse fiber diameter can reach more than 25μm, interweaving in the fiber structure to form a strong skeleton support, while its fine fiber can reach 3-10μm, filling in the skeleton to form a three-dimensional fiber mesh structure of coarse and fine spiral interweaving, which is the basis for its high filtration efficiency.",
      "• Good fluffiness: The high dust holding coarse denier melt-spun filter material has very good fluffiness due to its unique structure. The thickness can be from 0.6mm to 8mm, which gives it a huge dust holding advantage in HVAC applications.",
      "• Electrostatic electret property : The high dust holding coarse denier melt-spun filter material product uses polypropylene as the main raw material and has electrostatic electret property. Through the electret process, it can have a higher electrostatic adsorption property, so that it can have a very high interception efficiency for fine dust particles below 1μm through electrostatic adsorption on the basis of basic structure filtration.",
      "• Larger weight range: High dust holding coarse denier melt-spun filter material products have a larger weight range, with a minimum weight of 30g/m2 and a maximum weight of 400g/m2. It has a wide adaptability and different weights can be selected according to different application requirements.",
      "• Short processing steps: High dust holding coarse denier melt-spinning filter material is a pure filament process. The raw materials used are mainly thermoplastic resins, which are made by melt spinning. It has the characteristics of short processing flow, one-time molding and high output.",
      "High dust holding coarse denier melt-spun filter materials can be widely used in wire mesh supported filters, plate self-supporting filters, bag filters and other products due to their excellent filtering performance.",
      "The on-site response was enthusiastic and they talked about the future together",
      "At the report sharing site, Li Hongchang, the technical engineering manager of ZFT Group, explained in an easy-to-understand manner the technical details and application cases of high dust holding coarse denier meltblown filter materials, which aroused great interest among the audience. The audience took out their mobile phones to take photos and record, and many industry colleagues seized the opportunity to actively ask questions and conduct in-depth discussions on material performance optimization, process and other aspects. After the meeting, many participants took the initiative to add contact information, looking forward to deeper cooperation and exchanges in the future.",
